    <div class="prop-card" id="card-PROP-2026-06-25-002" style="display:none">
      <div style="background:#a0306a18;border-left:4px solid #a0306a;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:0 6px 0 0">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#a0306a;letter-spacing:.05em">BARBARA FREDRICKSON · PAPER · 2025</div>
        <div style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:#222;margin:4px 0 2px">Interparental positivity spillover theory: How parents' positive relational interactions influence children</div>
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.1177/17456916231220626" target="_blank" style="font-size:11px;color:#a0306a;opacity:.8">https://doi.org/10.1177/17456916231220626</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:16px 18px">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">SUMMARY</div>
        <div style="font-size:13px;color:#333;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px">Don, Simpson, Fredrickson & Algoe propose "interparental positivity spillover theory" in Perspectives on Psychological Science: a framework for how positive relational interactions *between* parents (including positivity resonance) transmit beyond the dyad to shape children's development. It extends broaden-and-build and positivity-resonance theory from a within-dyad mechanism to a multi-person, cross-generational transmission process.</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">WHY IT MATTERS</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#444;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px">The positivity-resonance program has been overwhelmingly dyadic. This is a theory-level extension to a *system* — how resonance in one relationship propagates to third parties who are not direct participants in the resonant moment. That propagation logic is exactly what C2A2 needs to model (how resonance inside one tradition-community radiates to observers/apprentices), so this is a high-value structural addition, not just another empirical study.</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin:12px 0 4px">CANDIDATE PRS TRIPLETS</div>
        
        <div style="border-left:3px solid #a0306a;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;background:#fafafa;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CANDIDATE PRS 1 — <span style="background:#1a6b3c;color:#fff;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700">High</span></div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#c0392b;width:14px;display:inline-block">P</span> Broaden-and-build and positivity resonance describe effects within an interacting dyad, but offer no account of how the benefits of a resonant relationship reach people who are not parties to the interaction.</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#2a6496;width:14px;display:inline-block">R</span> Interparental positivity spillover theory — a model of the pathways (emotional, behavioral, relational-climate) by which positive interaction between two partners influences a third party (the child).</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#1a6b3c;width:14px;display:inline-block">S</span> Positive relational quality is reframed as a system-level resource with spillover pathways, establishing that positivity resonance has indirect, propagating effects beyond the resonant dyad.</div>
          <div style="margin-top:5px;font-size:11px;color:#666;font-style:italic">Evidence: The paper's stated thesis and title — positive interactions between parents influence children via specified spillover pathways (Perspectives on Psychological Science, 2025).</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12px"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CROSS-TRADITION SIGNALS</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#444">- **C2A2 core relevance:** spillover pathways are a candidate mechanism for how a richly resonant community transmits its "feel" to newcomers climbing toward maturity in the tradition — resonance as a propagating, not merely dyadic, community resource.
- **Levin:** spillover/propagation across a relational network echoes the scale-up question (how local coupling produces higher-order collective states) in basal-cognition terms.
- **McGilchrist:** transmitted relational climate as an environment that shapes the attentional/affective stance a developing person brings to the world.
- **Stump:** parallels the Thomistic "united-something-or-other" / corporate-substance line (Stump P14–P16) — the family as a formed composite whose internal relations causally shape its members.</div></div>
      </div>
