    <div class="prop-card" id="card-PROP-2026-06-25-003" style="display:none">
      <div style="background:#a0306a18;border-left:4px solid #a0306a;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:0 6px 0 0">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#a0306a;letter-spacing:.05em">BARBARA FREDRICKSON · PAPER · 2025</div>
        <div style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:#222;margin:4px 0 2px">High-quality listening behaviors linked to social connection between strangers</div>
        <a href="https://peplab.web.unc.edu/articles-and-chapters/" target="_blank" style="font-size:11px;color:#a0306a;opacity:.8">https://peplab.web.unc.edu/articles-and-chapters/</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:16px 18px">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">SUMMARY</div>
        <div style="font-size:13px;color:#333;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px">West, Huston, Chandler, Zhou & Fredrickson (in press, Communications Psychology) provide a behavioral test of the claim that high-quality listening enables positive connection between strangers. The study links observable listening behaviors to social connection in stranger interactions, specifying listening as a manipulable behavioral lever for positivity resonance with people outside one's existing ties.</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">WHY IT MATTERS</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#444;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px">The wiki already holds the *conceptual* claim that high-quality listening is a resonance enabler (P8, from the UBC colloquium and Zhou & Fredrickson 2023). This is the distinct, not-yet-captured *behavioral* paper that ties specific listening behaviors to connection between strangers — i.e., it operationalizes the lever. Stranger-connection is the empirical analogue of cross-tradition first contact, so this is unusually direct C2A2 grounding.</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin:12px 0 4px">CANDIDATE PRS TRIPLETS</div>
        
        <div style="border-left:3px solid #a0306a;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;background:#fafafa;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CANDIDATE PRS 1 — <span style="background:#1a6b3c;color:#fff;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700">High</span></div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#c0392b;width:14px;display:inline-block">P</span> High-quality listening is hypothesized to enable positivity resonance with strangers, but which concrete, observable listening behaviors do the work — and whether they actually produce connection between strangers — needed behavioral evidence.</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#2a6496;width:14px;display:inline-block">R</span> A behavioral study coding high-quality listening behaviors and relating them to measured social connection in stranger dyads.</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#1a6b3c;width:14px;display:inline-block">S</span> Specific high-quality listening behaviors are empirically linked to social connection between strangers, identifying listening as a trainable behavioral pathway to weak-tie / stranger positivity resonance.</div>
          <div style="margin-top:5px;font-size:11px;color:#666;font-style:italic">Evidence: The paper's title claim and design — high-quality listening behaviors linked to social connection between strangers (Communications Psychology, in press).</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12px"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CROSS-TRADITION SIGNALS</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#444">- **C2A2 core relevance (flag strongly):** stranger-to-stranger connection via trainable listening behavior is a direct candidate intervention for first encounters between members of rival traditions — the behavioral on-ramp to "second-first-language" receptivity.
- **McGilchrist:** high-quality listening as right-hemisphere-style open, receptive attention to the other — a convergent-construct bridge already on the watch-list.
- **Friston:** attentive listening as active sampling that tightens mutual prediction between strangers.
- **Stump:** listening as the behavioral entry to Franciscan / second-person knowledge of persons (Stump P10–P11) — knowing-by-encounter rather than by proposition.</div></div>
      </div>
