        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">SUMMARY</div>
        <div style="font-size:13px;color:#333;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px">Wolfram's biweekly unscripted Q&A (1h16m), the first Future-of-Science-&-Technology
livestream after the captured May 15 episode. Across the session he fields questions on
whether hyper-personalized technology could leave two people effectively "living in
different realities," whether AI agents will become sovereign quasi-jurisdictions, whether
minds are computable (whole-brain emulation, personal identity, brain-to-brain linking),
and where the real bottleneck on progress lies — lack of knowledge, lack of computation, or
lack of conceptual frameworks.</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">WHY IT MATTERS</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#444;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px">These are Wolfram applying his standing apparatus — observer-dependent sampling of the
Ruliad, computational irreducibility, the rulial space of minds — to live questions about
mind-uploading, personal identity, and the structure of scientific progress. The
"different-realities" and "bottleneck on progress" threads are the program's two most
C2A2-relevant signals to surface since the April 3 Q&A (PRS-15/16).</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin:12px 0 4px">CANDIDATE PRS TRIPLETS</div>
        
        <div style="border-left:3px solid #4a006a;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;background:#fafafa;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CANDIDATE PRS 1 — <span style="background:#8a4a00;color:#fff;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700">Medium</span></div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#c0392b;width:14px;display:inline-block">P</span> If observers sample the Ruliad differently (PRS-05/17), what happens when
    technology actively widens the divergence between two human observers' samplings?</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#2a6496;width:14px;display:inline-block">R</span> Wolfram's "two people effectively living in different realities" framing — a
    technologically-amplified case of observer-dependent reality.</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#1a6b3c;width:14px;display:inline-block">S</span> Recasts hyper-personalization as a rulial-space divergence between observers,
    making "incommensurable effective realities" a consequence of the observer theory rather
    than a mere social worry — and naming a failure mode for any shared knowledge commons.</div>
          <div style="margin-top:5px;font-size:11px;color:#666;font-style:italic">Evidence: Q&A segment on personalized technology and divergent realities (per livestream
    description).</div>
        </div>
        <div style="border-left:3px solid #4a006a;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;background:#fafafa;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CANDIDATE PRS 2 — <span style="background:#8a4a00;color:#fff;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700">Medium</span></div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#c0392b;width:14px;display:inline-block">P</span> How should we model the rate-limiting step on scientific/technological progress —
    the question C2A2's whole measurement aim turns on?</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#2a6496;width:14px;display:inline-block">R</span> Wolfram's trichotomy of bottlenecks: lack of knowledge vs. lack of computation
    vs. lack of conceptual frameworks; plus his "person / team / AI-assisted computational
    process" framing of where the next breakthrough comes from.</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#1a6b3c;width:14px;display:inline-block">S</span> Supplies a concrete candidate taxonomy for what a progress metric must score — and
    foregrounds "conceptual frameworks" (new paradigms / new questions) as a distinct,
    possibly dominant bottleneck, which aligns tightly with the PRS-triplet thesis that
    progress is chained problem→resource→solution moves.</div>
          <div style="margin-top:5px;font-size:11px;color:#666;font-style:italic">Evidence: Q&A segment on whether the bottleneck is knowledge, computation, or conceptual
    frameworks (per livestream description).</div>
        </div>
        <div style="border-left:3px solid #4a006a;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;background:#fafafa;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CANDIDATE PRS 3 — <span style="background:#7a1a1a;color:#fff;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700">Speculative</span></div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#c0392b;width:14px;display:inline-block">P</span> Are minds computable, and if so what survives copying/uploading — i.e., where do
    persons sit in the rulial space of minds (PRS-03/05/17)?</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#2a6496;width:14px;display:inline-block">R</span> Wolfram's live treatment of whole-brain emulation, mind-computability, personal
    identity, and brain-to-brain linking as questions about an observer's path through the
    Ruliad.</div>
          <div style="margin:3px 0"><span style="font-weight:900;color:#1a6b3c;width:14px;display:inline-block">S</span> Extends the rulial-space-of-minds agenda from abstract observer-classes (PRS-17)
    to the concrete case of human personal identity under copying/merging, where identity
    becomes a question about continuity of a rulial path rather than substrate.</div>
          <div style="margin-top:5px;font-size:11px;color:#666;font-style:italic">Evidence: Q&A segment on whole-brain emulation, minds being computable, personal identity,
    and linking brains (per livestream description).</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12px"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#888;margin-bottom:4px">CROSS-TRADITION SIGNALS</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#444">- **Hoffman / Kastrup** — PRS-CANDIDATE-01 is a live instance of the open index question
  "Is Wolfram's observer-dependent spacetime the computational equivalent of Hoffman's
  fitness interface?" Technologically-amplified divergent realities is a shared object for
